[E-PROP-ELIM] Error: can't match on a proof of `Exists` to produce data
   ╭─[ reject/proof-tuple-exists-to-data.sw:5:7 ]
   │
 5 │   let (n, _) := h
   │       ───┬──  
   │          ╰──── can't match on a proof of `Exists` to produce data
   │ 
   │ Note: `Exists` is a proposition, so its proofs are erased at runtime. Matching on one can only produce data when the proposition has at most one constructor and every field is itself a proof. A tuple pattern is `Witness` written shorter (`(n, p)` is `Witness n p`), so it isn't a way out
